# sticky_proxy_resolver.py - Strict Geo-Consistency & Sticky Proxy Resolver Engine
# Resolves, validates, and clamps proxy routing to match the persona's original registration region
#
# CHANGELOG (iter9 - deep audit fixes, see STICKY_PROXY_RESOLVER_DEEP_DIVE_R1.md):
#   SPR1  - Wired resolver methods into orchestrator. The class was
#          imported and instantiated but NONE of its methods were
#          called. The proxy URL flowed directly from
#          get_socks5_url_for_persona() to the browser without any
#          geo-verification, clamping, or backup fallback.
#   SPR2  - check_proxy_integrity() is now called before browser launch.
#          Was: defined but never called.
#   SPR3  - HTTPS for all intelligence queries. ip-api.com fallback
#          was using plain HTTP, leaking DNS to local resolver.
#   SPR4  - compile_dynamic_sticky_proxy_string() now accepts a
#          country parameter. Non-US personas (london, paris, berlin)
#          now produce valid proxy strings.
#   SPR5  - Added local MaxMind GeoLite2-style fallback. External
#          intelligence services (ipinfo.io, ip-api.com) are now
#          secondary; they are well-known anti-bot signals.
#   SPR6  - Cache keyed by IP, not URL. For rotating residential
#          proxies, the IP changes per request but the URL stays
#          the same. Previous cache missed every time.
#   SPR7  - LRU eviction via collections.OrderedDict. Previous FIFO
#          evicted most-used entries first.
#   SPR8  - TTL-based cache entries (10 minutes). Previous cache
#          returned stale data indefinitely.
#   SPR11 - X-Forwarded-For and Via header stripping in outgoing
#          requests. Prevents container IP leak.
#   SPR12 - TLS fingerprint impersonation via curl_cffi for
#          intelligence queries. Avoids Python JA3 fingerprint
#          being detected.
#   SPR13 - Shared httpx client (connection pooling). New client
#          per call triggered rate-limiting.
#   SPR14 - Retry with exponential backoff. Rate-limited endpoints
#          now retry with delays.
#   SPR15 - HTTPS for all intelligence queries.
#   SPR16 - lock_persona parameter for match_persona_to_proxy_location().
#          Mutates persona fields only on first binding.
#   SPR17 - Type-check conn parameter for asyncpg.Connection.
#   SPR18 - UUID4 session IDs. Previous 6-digit session IDs had
#          collision risk.
#   SPR19 - Session ID cached by persona_id. Sticky across calls.
#   SPR20 - compile_dynamic_sticky_proxy_string() wired into orchestrator.
#
# CHANGELOG (iter13 - fifth-pass audit fixes, see STICKY_PROXY_RESOLVER_DEEP_DIVE_R2.md):
#   SPR21 - Fuzzy geo matching: "Dallas" matches "Plano" if both in
#          the same region. State-level fallback when city match fails.
#   SPR22 - Cache egress IP resolution result (was: 1 req per call).
#   SPR23 - Fallback path limits to 3 iterations. Circuit-breaker:
#          skip geo check after 3 consecutive failures.
#   SPR24 - Document api.ipify.org as anti-bot signal.
#   SPR25 - Use ipinfo.io for BOTH health check and geo lookup
#          (was: different endpoints, inconsistent results).
#   SPR26 - Use urllib.parse.urlparse for proper URL parsing (was:
#          manual split, breaks on @ in password).
#   SPR27 - URL-decode password after parsing.
#   SPR29 - Register atexit cleanup. Document that panic handler
#          bypasses cleanup.
#   SPR30 - Generate NEW session ID for fallback proxy (was: kept
#          primary's session ID, defeating stickiness).
#   SPR31 - Normalize city names (St. → Saint) for ILIKE matching.
#   SPR32 - Validate fingerprint structure before using it.
#   SPR35 - Differentiate "proxy dead" vs "geo unknown". Use primary
#          if health check passed but geo unknown.
#   SPR36 - __del__ method with cleanup warning.
#   SPR37 - Validate city parameter is non-empty.
#
# CHANGELOG (iter15 - sixth-pass audit fixes, see STICKY_PROXY_RESOLVER_DEEP_DIVE_R3.md):
#   SPR39 - __del__ is now total-safe (try/except AttributeError).
#          Previously crashed during interpreter shutdown if called
#          before __init__ finished.
#   SPR40 - LRU off-by-one fixed (>= 1000 not > 1000).
#   SPR41 - threading.Lock protects counter + cache mutations. Defends
#          against atexit/sync __del__ crossing event-loop boundaries.
#   SPR42 - health_check_proxy also extracts city/region/timezone from
#          ipinfo.io and PRIMES the cache. Halves the intelligence
#          call volume (1 request instead of 2 for IP+geo).
#   SPR43 - Centralized circuit-breaker logic with TTL on open state
#          (5 min). Auto-resets to allow probe.
#   SPR44 - Shared httpx client uses trust_env=False. Prevents
#          reading HTTP_PROXY/HTTPS_PROXY from the environment,
#          which would route the resolver's intelligence queries
#          through the system proxy or local DNS (DNS leak).
#   SPR45 - _strip_proxy_headers is now a public static method (was
#          dead code). Defense-in-depth helper for future header
#          injection.
#   SPR47 - _make_sticky_session_id raises ValueError on empty
#          persona_id (defense against upstream bugs).
#   SPR48 - Session-ID cache capped at 4 entries (1 + 3 backups).
#   SPR49 - Typed exceptions ProxyUnavailableError and GeoBreachError
#          replace bare ValueError. Orchestrator can now distinguish
#          "no proxy alive" from "geo mismatch".
#   SPR50 - get_proxy_for_persona wrapped in asyncio.wait_for(60s).
#          Hard upper bound prevents DoS.
#   SPR51 - Single attempt per endpoint (no retries). Previously made
#          6 rapid requests to intelligence APIs, which is itself
#          an anti-bot fingerprint.
#   SPR52 - Timezone reconciliation: compares proxy's actual timezone
#          (from ipinfo) to persona's expected timezone. Mismatches
#          are logged as warnings (reCAPTCHA Enterprise top-3 signal).
#   SPR53 - health_check_proxy now also trips the circuit-breaker on
#          failure (not just geo failures).
#   SPR54 - IPv6-aware proxy URL construction. Brackets the host
#          when it's an IPv6 address. Detects via ipaddress.IPv6Address.
#   SPR55 - Cache key strategy documented: URL-keyed cache holds
#          the last seen egress IP; IP-keyed cache holds the geo.
#          No collision risk for rotating vs static proxies.
#   SPR56 - Shared client uses a Chrome 120 User-Agent header. The
#          default python-httpx UA is an instant Python automation
#          signal.
#   SPR57 - City name is URL-encoded in the proxy username (handles
#          Unicode accents and special characters).
#   SPR58 - PID-budget decision documented: 3 concurrent httpx
#          requests stay under the 128 PID budget.
#   SPR59 - health_check_proxy accepts expected_egress_ip parameter.
#          Verifies the actual egress IP matches expectations
#          (defends against transparent proxies / NAT).
#   SPR60 - Circuit-breaker is in-memory only (not persisted across
#          daemon restarts). Documented as intentional.
#   SPR61 - match_persona_to_proxy_location uses exact match
#          (signup_geo_region = $1) instead of ILIKE '%$1%'. The
#          fuzzy state-level fallback is in _fuzzy_geo_match.
#   SPR62 - 1 quick in-call retry on transient health-check failures
#          (was: 0 retries; orchestrator had to retry the whole task).
#
# CHANGELOG (iter17 - seventh-pass audit fixes, see STICKY_PROXY_RESOLVER_DEEP_DIVE_R4.md):
#   SPR63 - Re-compilation bug: detect and strip existing city-locked
#          markers (-country-...-session-...) from the username before
#          appending new ones. Prevents doubly-nested params when the
#          orchestrator's retry path passes an already-compiled URL
#          back through compile_dynamic_sticky_proxy_string().
#   SPR64 - Documented state-level false positive risk: "Dallas" and
#          "El Paso" are both TX, but 600 miles apart. The fuzzy
#          match currently treats them as the same region. The fix
#          is in the orchestrator: it should pass a tighter geo
#          (e.g., zip code) when binding critical personas.
#   SPR65 - _infer_country_from_geo now returns actual country code
#          (us/ca/gb/jp/au/...) instead of always 'us'. Maps 50 US
#          states, 50 US state abbrevs, and 80+ non-US countries/
#          provinces/states.
#   SPR66 - _normalize_city_name: documented that 'St.' is interpreted
#          as 'Saint' even when it means 'Street'. The function is
#          only called for city names, so this is theoretical.
#   SPR67 - Canonical proxy URL normalization for cache key consistency.
#          Bracket IPv6 hosts, lowercase scheme, strip default ports,
#          and remove IPv6 zone IDs. The cache key is now computed on
#          the canonical form, so logically equivalent URLs map to
#          the same key.
#   SPR68 - Don't pollute the cache with 'unknown' geo entries. A
#          subsequent call should retry the lookup, not return the
#          same 'unknown' from the cache.
#   SPR69 - get_proxy_for_persona and _find_backup_proxy accept
#          expected_egress_ip parameter. Passed through to
#          health_check_proxy for transparent-proxy / NAT detection.
#   SPR70 - compile_dynamic_sticky_proxy_string logs at WARNING
#          (not ERROR) when returning the base URL on exception.
#          Caller can now detect silent failures via log scraping.
#   SPR71 - _make_sticky_session_id: documented that the session ID
#          is added to the cache BEFORE the URL is fully built. If
#          URL construction fails, the orphaned session ID is
#          harmless (next call with same persona_id returns same ID).
#   SPR72 - match_persona_to_proxy_location now tries multiple
#          city forms (raw, normalized, lowercase) for the DB
#          exact-match query. Handles DBs that store "Plano" vs
#          "Plano, Texas".
#   SPR73 - health_check_proxy: egress_ip_match defaults to True
#          when expected_egress_ip is None. Consistent with the
#          "no verification needed" semantics.
#   SPR74 - get_proxy_for_persona retry state isolation: the
#          circuit-breaker counter is rolled back if the second
#          attempt of a retry pair succeeds. Prevents a single
#          transient failure from polluting breaker state.
#   SPR75 - _strip_proxy_headers: documented as defense-in-depth
#          for future custom header injection. Not called in the
#          current code because the shared client doesn't inject
#          leaky headers.
#   SPR76 - IPv6 zone ID handling: _canonicalize_proxy_url strips
#          '%zone' suffix from IPv6 hosts before bracket-wrapping.
#          RFC 6874 zone IDs are unusual for residential proxies
#          but possible for link-local addresses.
#   SPR77 - All internal HTTP calls have explicit timeouts. The
#          outer asyncio.wait_for(60s) is the hard upper bound.
#   SPR78 - Cache writes are atomic within each method (single
#          lock acquisition covers both URL-keyed and IP-keyed
#          entries).
#   SPR79 - compile_dynamic_sticky_proxy_string validates country
#          code against ISO 3166-1 alpha-2 set. Invalid codes
#          fall back to 'us' with a warning.
#   SPR80 - Cache size cap (1000) is already enforced. No change.
#   SPR82 - asyncpg rolls back uncommitted transactions on context
#          exit, so match_persona_to_proxy_location's None returns
#          are safe (no DB state pollution).

